# What sql_alert_transitions() hands its callback of an entry's columns, as C reads each: a NULL and an empty
# text in every text column (the alarm's, the entry's and the rule's); a value stored as NULL (what C's save
# makes of a NaN: it binds the double, and SQLite stores a NaN as NULL), infinities, a zero with a sign, an
# integer; statuses, a delay and an exit code read as C's int (negative ones, -1, numbers above 32 bits, a
# status with a fraction); flags, times and an alarm id above 32 bits and negative; texts with bytes the vectors
# escape, and one longer than any cut of the endpoint; a global id that is NULL and one that is negative.
database real
